# <file system>        <mount pt>    <type>  <options>                                         <dump> <pass>
# /data is not here: the boot entry names it (systemd.mount-extra), so this file is the same on every disk.
# Not an automount: with no drive, every look at /media/songs used to wait 3 s for it, and YARG looks at thousands of paths
# in its song cache (a scan took hours). The drive is mounted by udev when it appears (71-yargos-songs.rules) and unmounted
# when it goes (device-bound); with no drive /media/songs is an empty folder and every lookup fails at once.
LABEL=YARGSONGS        /media/songs  auto    ro,noatime,nofail,noauto,x-systemd.device-bound   0  0
tmpfs                  /tmp          tmpfs   mode=1777,nosuid,nodev                            0      0
